  "kind": "build",
  "title": "# Build: live-sessions-plugin (Opus, high thinking; plugin + widget, uses AmberX recorder) ## What …",
  "asked": "# Build: live-sessions-plugin (Opus, high thinking; plugin + widget, uses AmberX recorder) ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"Make a plugin with a widget that lists the active Claude accounts only. The ones that actually have a human involved, either this one or the helper. It needs to list any account that's actively being run, any session being run by a human, and then you can click a button and you can watch its output live, including voice. It will be able to hear you talking to me, and me talking to you.\" Asked whether the person on a watched session should know: \"You can have it: 'you're being watched'.\" This **replaces the parked Plan Studio idea 'Claude sessions list (Molly plugin)'** (id claude-sessions-list-molly-plugin-wpo6). Mark that plan as superseded and link it to this build. Book to a free named agent. ## Do 1. **Plugin 'Live sessions'** (`plugin@1`, `forFramework: true` so its commands get Molly voice commands automatically), installable in the console, Molly, AmberX web and axHub web. 2. **Detect human-driven sessions only**, across Brett's main account and any helper accounts (handoff-2): interactive Claude Code terminals, claude.ai chats/voice calls using the axHub connector, and the AmberX/Gizmo companion. **Exclude headless `claude -p` builds and agent-swarm jobs.** Use session-checkin, the axHub connector activity per account, Terminal sessions and the handoff session channel. Show account, device, app, what it's on right now, how long, and whether it's voice or text. 3. **Widget** (attachable to toolbar, main bar, nav, any window title bar via 'Add widgets…'): a count plus avatars of live human sessions. Click opens the list. Each row has a **Watch live** button. 4. **Watch live**: a panel/window streaming that session's output live (messages, tool calls and results, build status) and **voice: both sides**, the human's speech and Claude's replies, via **AmberX's Audio Output Recorder (+ mic) on the device running the session**, streamed through axHub. Live transcript under the audio. Play/pause, mute, volume, jump to live, pop out, and a recording toggle (off by default). - If that device doesn't have AmberX paired, show text-only with 'Voice needs AmberX on that phone' and the setup steps. 5. **'You're being watched' indicator** on the watched session's side whenever anyone is watching: an AmberX overlay/notification, a console/Molly banner chip, and a line posted in the Breakroom Sessions chat naming who's watching. It turns off when the last watcher leaves. Always on, not optional. 6. Owner-only to watch (primary). Helpers can see the list but can't watch the primary. Every watch start/stop is audit-logged. 7. Settings via settings-interface@1. Live updates via handoff-2's push stream (coordinate, don't build a second one). 8. Tests, UI Review shots (non-blocking), PR, auto-land, redeploy. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. ## ADDENDUM 1 (Brett, voice, Nov 4): overrides step 2's 'human only' and step 4's scope \"Actually, make it list all sessions, but note whether it's a human or a headless. Only allow voice monitoring of the human.\" - **List ALL Claude sessions**: human-driven AND headless (`claude -p` builds, agent-swarm jobs, Gizmo background work), across all accounts. Each row has a clear **Human / Headless** badge (icon + label), plus agent/crew name for headless (Joey, Rhonda...), the build/step it's on, model, thinking, time and cost. - Filters: All / Human / Headless, by account, by agent. The widget count can show both ('2 human · 4 headless'). - **Watch live (text output)** works for every session, human or headless (headless streams its build log/tool calls). - **Voice monitoring ONLY for human sessions.** The voice controls don't exist on headless rows. - 'You're being watched' still fires on human sessions whenever anyone watches (text or voice). Headless sessions just log the watch. ## ADDENDUM 2 (Brett, voice, Nov 4): grid + agent identity per session \"…",
